WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:10.250
Passion, dedication, and barely enough money
to buy a used sofa on Craigslist: these are

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.730
the things fan films are made of.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:18.130
Let's recognize the hard work and talent that
went into some of the best ones.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.929
Batman versus the Terminator

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:26.210
When all hope is lost and humanity’s demise
is certain, here comes the one man crazy enough

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.359
to fight murder-robots while dressed as a
bat.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.190
“You picking this up Jon”

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.730
The result is Batman versus the Terminator.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.289
In this animated short, not only do fans get
an older, tough-as-nails Batman inspired by

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:48.670
the works of Frank Miller...they also get
Batman mowing down T-800 robo-skeletons in

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:54.579
his Bat-tank in the post-apocalyptic, machine-controlled
Earth from the Terminator movies.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:56.239
Death Scene Springtrap

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.890
In the Five Nights At Freddy's games, players
control a newly hired security guard at a

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.829
Chuck E.
Cheese-like restaurant.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:07.820
It's a quiet night and everything's going
normally, until the creepy animatronic animal

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.000
characters come to life.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.710
This fan film adaptation of the game isn’t
even a minute and a half long and yet it still

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.030
manages to capture every detail that makes
the game series great.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.720
Spawn: The Recall

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.310
In 1997, Spawn hit the big screen—and it
was a disaster.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.050
“Spawny, Spawny he’s our man if he can’t
kill em no one can.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.040
Yeah”

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.960
The fan film Spawn: The Recall, succeeds where
Spawn '97 failed.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:41.880
In it, a child and his mother come face-to-face
with Spawn himself, who has a dire message

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.180
that must be delivered.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.410
“Lucifer is back”

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.259
Fans nailed Spawn in eight minutes.

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:53.380
The best Hollywood could do was...this.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.250
“That face for me.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.250
Oops”

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.250
Our RoboCop Remake

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:03.130
Our RoboCop Remake was an attempt to re-create
or reimagine every scene from the original

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.610
1987 RoboCop movie.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:11.470
Dozens of Los Angeles-area comedians and sketch
groups each picked one scene to make as they

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.470
pleased.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:18.160
In the end, all of their stylistically different
work was stitched together to form one utterly

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.020
unique RoboCop.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.440
And it didn't need Michael Keaton or Samuel
L. Jackson, either.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.440
Dirty Laundry

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.720
Marvel’s 2004 Punisher movie was a letdown.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.770
Star Thomas Jane more than made up for it
by reprising his role as the vigilante in

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:35.910
a short fan film called Dirty Laundry.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:41.420
All of Frank Castle's rage and capacity for
lethal violence is unleashed when a normal

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.690
laundry day is interrupted by gang violence.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.930
It's brutal, bloody, and actually fun to watch.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.550
Batman: Dead End

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:56.440
Just when a showdown between Batman and the
Joker is about to peak, a new fighter enters

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:02.050
the match: a Xenomorph, the acid-drooling
monster from the Alien movies.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.950
The alien pins Batman …and then someone
else shows up.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:06.950
And some others.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.120
It doesn't make much sense, but it's awesome.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.210
Severus Snape and the Marauders

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:19.690
Set in 1978, this 25-minute film tells the
story of James Potter—Harry's dad— Sirius

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:25.030
Black, Peter Pettigrew, and Remus Lupin, as
they bully young Severus Snape after he tries

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.030
to meet Lily in a bar.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:32.540
It perfectly captures Snape's inner rage and
conflict as a man who walks the line between

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.580
good and evil.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.580
Troops

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:45.050
“Come for you, Tell me what you wanna do,
whats you gonna do”

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:50.700
If there were a fan-film hall of fame, Troops
would be an immediate inductee.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:57.480
Made in 1997, it's an episode of COPS set
in the Star Wars universe, starring dimwitted

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.590
Stormtroopers on Tatooine.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.870
It's groundbreaking for its use of impressive
low-budget CG effects.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:08.010
Even better?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.010
It's really funny.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.010
Power/Rangers

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.570
Part fan-film remake and part parody of dark,
gritty reboots, Power/Rangers takes the kiddie

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:20.470
franchise and tells how each Ranger has spiraled
downward in their Ranger-retirements.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:25.820
It has a lot more money behind it than most
fan films, and more star power, too, with

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:31.560
appearances from James van der Beek and Battlestar
Galactica's Katee Sackhoff.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.860
Star Wars: Uncut

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:40.560
Star Wars fan Casey Pugh had a wild idea:
a crowdsourced shot-for-shot remake of A New

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.560
Hope.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:46.750
Fans claimed 15-second segments of the film
to remake, and then Pugh edited them together.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:51.720
One moment Han, Luke, and Obi-Wan are Legos,
and seconds later it's a bunch of kids in

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.790
their backyards with broom handles for lightsabers.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:05:01.090
A fresh take on a familiar classic, it adds
up to one of the best fan films ever.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:06.200
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.760
And leave us a comment to let us know which fan film you're a fan of...

